    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-03, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (116 hits across 27 queries, scan regenerated 2026-11-03 06:0x KST via 'bash run.sh scan', 0 source errors, collected_at 2026-11-02T21:0x UTC). The score-9 top band was ENTIRELY RECYCLED for the eighth consecutive cycle (GSE328275 TNBC-CD45 immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential lymph-node metastasis spatial, GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G opioid CosMx, GSE346380 / GSE348495 CosMx lung and colorectal resources, GSE288340 post-CAR-T marrow spatial atlas, GSE311507 HNSCC dependency map, and the GSE281462/64/65 3D-chromatin-GWAS bundle), so the actionable harvest comes from the score-7 and score-6 ladder. Dedupe was performed at ACCESSION level against the full git history of the digest page (390 distinct GSE accessions have ever appeared in any commit of src/app/digest/page.tsx), not merely against the visible 5-entry window - this is the stricter test, and 24 candidate accessions in today's scan survived the archive-wide check. All three picks below have NEVER appeared in any digest commit, and each was verified against its live NCBI GEO esummary record (title, depositor summary, taxon, sample count, pdat, gds_type, supplementary files) rather than title-matching alone. Signal 1 is GSE346602 (Mus musculus, n=7, pdat 2026/11/01, H5AD + TXT): a full-length humanized MPZL2 knock-in mouse carrying the MPZL2 c.220C>T East-Asian founder variant (FL-hMPZL2Q74X/Q74X) that recapitulates nonsense-mediated decay seen in patient-derived cells and reproduces progressive hearing loss more faithfully than the authors' earlier cDNA knock-in model, with sequential pathology from Deiters' cell disorganization to Deiters'-outer-hair-cell degeneration; an optimized dual-AAV-ie-K558R system encoding a PAM-flexible ABE8eWQ-SpRY base editor restores auditory function after hearing onset and remains effective at post-maturation stages, delivering significant recovery when hearing loss is substantial but Deiters' cell architecture is still preserved - and, critically, NO clear benefit once Deiters' cell disorganization has begun despite comparable on-target editing efficiency. Signal 2 is GSE352361 (n=8) + GSE352362 (n=15, TSV + XLSX): matched bulk skeletal-muscle and quadriceps RNA-seq in Nfe2l1 muscle-specific knockout mice under rapamycin (mTOR inhibition) and rolipram (PDE4 inhibition) treatment, framing proteostasis failure and muscle pathology as the drug-response substrate. Signal 3 is GSE281661 (Mus musculus, n=6, pdat 2026/11/01, MTX + TSV): single-cell sequencing of METTL3 conditional-knockout and wild-type tumour tissue (3 cases per genotype) showing METTL3 as the driver of FAP-tagged inflammatory CAF generation and maintenance, with poor prognosis in patients; mechanistically METTL3 enhances m6A modification of RUFY1 and increases its mRNA stability via IGF2BP3 recognition, RUFY1 activates RAB4A-mediated endosomal signalling to drive secretion of the pro-tumour cytokines CXCL12, CXCL14 and IL-16, and CXCL12/CXCL14-CXCR4 activation of AKT reinforces both M2 macrophage polarization and tumor-promoting fibroblast transformation. What links the three is a single thesis for the day: THE PRODUCTIVE UNIT IS THE RESOLVABLE WINDOW - each signal identifies the interval in which the intervention still works (Signal 1: between hearing loss and Deiters' cell loss; Signal 2: between proteostasis failure and irreversible muscle pathology; Signal 3: between CAF m6A reprogramming and established immunosuppressive remodelling), and each supplies a matched intervention point plus a measured readout for whether the window is still open.",
